/**
\class pdg::Camera
\brief Animated view shared by ports and layers.

Scene-owned cameras advance on their scene clock. Layer overrides remain available;
\ref pdg::Scene describes ownership and pause behavior.

See \ref camera_output for camera visibility, composed opacity, fades and crossfades.

Camera also inherits EventEmitter. Subscribe on the camera, rather than on a
layer, to receive eventType_ZoomComplete with CameraZoomInfo {camera, zoom}.
zoomTo() targets an absolute magnification; zoom() multiplies the starting zoom.
Queued factors resolve when the operation starts. Both emit once per completed
operation, including a zero-duration operation (synchronously unless queued or
delayed). Cancelled/replaced operations and setZoom() do not emit. Pausing the
schedule delays completion. Shared attachments do not duplicate notifications.

\note Include pdg/sys/camera.h, pdg/sys/events.h and pdg/sys/ieventhandler.h.

\code{.cpp}
class ZoomListener : public pdg::IEventHandler {
public:
    bool handleEvent(pdg::EventEmitter*, long type, void* data) noexcept override {
        if (type != pdg::eventType_ZoomComplete) return false;
        const auto& completion = *static_cast<pdg::CameraZoomInfo*>(data);
        // completion.camera identifies the camera; completion.zoom is its final zoom.
        return false;
    }
};
// The listener must outlive its registration when using default no-op refcounts.
ZoomListener listener;
pdg::Camera camera;
camera.addHandler(&listener, pdg::eventType_ZoomComplete);
camera.zoomTo(2, 0.5).andThen().zoom(0.5, 0.5);
// Detached cameras are advanced manually; attached cameras use the runtime clock.
camera.animate(1);
camera.removeHandler(&listener, pdg::eventType_ZoomComplete);
\endcode
*/
